tes.␀This radio can't run a temporary radio (needs an SX1262), so it can't serve updates.␀␀␀␀Highly experimental. This forwards the text, sender name and timestamp of every message your node receives to an MQTT broker, where anyone able to read the broker can read them. Direct messages are private messages from other people who never agreed to be shared. Use a broker you control, set an encryption key below, and never a public broker.␀␀␀I accept the privacy risk␀␀␀Enable MQTT bridge␀␀Broker␀␀Broker host / IP␀␀␀␀192.168.1.x␀Port␀␀␀␀1883␀␀␀␀Leave empty if not required␀Username (optional)␀Password (optional)␀Publish␀Publish channel messages␀␀␀␀Other people's private messages to you. Only to a broker you control.␀␀␀Publish direct messages␀Empty = plaintext to a private broker␀␀␀Encryption key (optional)␀␀␀psk␀Nothing above applies until you save.␀␀␀Internal DRAM
